spec gg06-delete-disjoint-parallel-edges: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# GG06 (disjoint parallel edges). Two parallel edges a->b (id 1, id 2) and a self-loop a->a (id 3).
# s1 deletes edge id 1, s2 deletes edge id 2, each by instance. The same instance:
# the second deleter is refused. Different instances: the catalogue expects both to
# commit; every instance here has source a, the node the adjacency conflict rule
# claims, so the golden pins which verdict holds.
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s1d s1c s2d s2c
step s1d: MATCH (:N {name:'a'})-[r:R {id:1}]->() DELETE r RETURN count(*) AS deleted
deleted
-------
1      
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2d: MATCH (:N {name:'a'})-[r:R {id:2}]->() DELETE r RETURN count(*) AS deleted
deleted
-------
1      
(1 row)
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: serialization conflict
final final: MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name
name
----
"a" 
"b" 
(2 rows)
final edges: MATCH (x)-[r]->(y) RETURN x.name AS src, r.id AS id, y.name AS dst ORDER BY src, id, dst
src|id|dst
---+--+---
"a"|2 |"b"
"a"|3 |"a"
(2 rows)
final dangling: <lpg: arcs touching a dead node, at a fresh snapshot>
live_arcs|dangling
---------+--------
2        |0       
(1 row)

